.TH MD2TROFF 1
.SH NAME
md2troff \- Markdown as troff's input, for book
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B md2troff
[
.BI -m " macros"
] [
.B -q
.BR gb | us | none
] [
.BI -k " key"
] [
.I file.md
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Md2troff
reads Markdown and writes troff for
.B -mbook
or a class built on it, named by
.B -m
or by
.B macros:
in the front matter:
.B book
(the default),
.BR article ,
.B memo
or
.BR slides .
.IR Book (1)
runs it on a book written in Markdown
.RI ( book .md
or
.IR book .markdown)
before it does anything else, so that
.EX
book paper.md
.EE
makes
.BR paper.pdf ,
tagged as any book's is.
The Markdown is CommonMark's, with GitHub's tables, task lists,
strikethrough and bare links, and pandoc's front matter, footnotes,
citations, mathematics, heading attributes, figures, fenced divs and
raw troff.
.SS The front matter
Between two lines
.B ---
at the head of the file, in YAML's form
.RB ( "key: value" ,
a list as
.B "- item"
lines or
.BR "[a, b]" ,
a long value as
.B "key: |"
and the lines indented under it):
.TP
.B "title  subtitle  date"
The title, a line of Markdown each.
.TP
.B author
A name, or a list of names, or of
.BR name ,
.BR affiliation ,
.BR email ,
.B location
and
.B extension
(a memorandum's room and telephone).
A book's authors are joined into one line.
.TP
.B abstract
Markdown, an article's or a memorandum's.
.TP
.B keywords
An article's.
.TP
.B lang
The language
.RB ( en-GB ),
in the PDF and for the quotation marks.
.TP
.B quotes
.BR gb ,
.B us
or
.B none
(below).
.TP
.B macros
The class, as
.BR -m .
.TP
.B numbersections
.B false
sets every heading unnumbered.
.TP
.B toc
.B true
sets the contents after the title.
.TP
.B notes
.B endnotes
sets the notes at the end
.RB ( .en ,
.BR .notes ).
.TP
.B "bibliography  citestyle"
The works cited and the style of the citations, for
.IR book 's
.B -p
and
.BR -S .
.TP
.B "papersize  columns"
The page, and an article's columns (1 or 2).
.TP
.B "org  case  file  number  kind  memotype  signature"
A memorandum's head, and
.B signature: true
its authors' names at its end.
.TP
.B "aspect  typeface"
A talk's
.RB ( 16:9
or
.BR 4:3 ;
.B sans
or
.BR serif ).
.PP
With no
.B title:
a lone heading of the first level at the head of the text is the
title.
.SS Blocks
Headings are
.BR .chapter ,
.BR .section ,
.B .subsection
and
.B .subsubsection
(in an article or memorandum
.BR .section ,
.B .subsection
and
.BR .subsubsection ;
in a talk
.B .section
and
.BR .slide ,
or
.B .slide
alone if the text has one level of heading): the highest level the
text has is the first, and a level deeper than the macros go is set
as their deepest.
A heading's attributes follow it in braces:
.B {#label}
its label for a cross-reference,
.B {-}
or
.B {.unnumbered}
unnumbered (the macro with
.BR * ),
.B {.appendix}
.B .appendix
before it.
.PP
Paragraphs are
.BR .p ;
block quotations
.BR .quote ;
lists
.B .list
(1, a, i or bullet, nested; a list that begins at another number, or
whose numbers end in
.BR ) ,
has its marks given; a task list's are ☐ and ☒); code, fenced or
indented,
.BR .code ;
a horizontal rule a centred
.B "* * *"
(in a talk, a new slide;
.B ". . ."
a pause).
A table is tbl's, its header in bold, its rules booktabs', a cell of
more than forty characters a block of text, the table then the
measure's width; with a caption (pandoc's
.B "Table: ..."
or
.BR ": ..." ,
before it or after, and a
.B {#label}
at its end) it is a floating
.BR .table .
An image alone in its paragraph is a
.BR .figure :
its text the caption, its title (or its text) the
.B .alt
that describes it in the tagged PDF,
.B {#label width=50% height=2in}
after it its label and size (a percentage of the measure, or
.BR in ,
.BR cm ,
.BR mm ,
.BR pt ,
.BR px ,
or troff's own units).
An image within a line is set as a figure after its paragraph, and
said.
.B $$
\&...
.B $$
is a display for eqn(1).
A fenced div
.RB ( ":::" )
of the class
.BR columns ,
.B column
.RB ( width= ),
.B epigraph
.RB ( attrib= ),
.B abstract
or
.B notes
(not set: a speaker's) is that; of any other, its text is set as it
is.
A code block fenced as
.B ```{=troff}
is troff, set as it is written; any other raw format is not set.
HTML is not set, and said; a comment is dropped.
.SS In the line
Emphasis is italic (roman within italic), strong emphasis bold, code
Libertinus Mono;
.BR ~~struck~~ ,
.B H~2~O
and
.B 2^10^
are struck, subscript and superscript.
A link is
.B .link
and a bare address
.BR .url ,
the punctuation after either joined to it.
A note,
.B [^name]
with its text elsewhere as
.B "[^name]: ..."
(its later paragraphs indented four spaces), or
.BR ^[text] ,
is a footnote
.RB ( .fn ),
or an endnote; a citation,
.BR "[@key, place; @key2]" ,
is
.B .cite
for
.IR refer (1),
a prefix before the
.B @
said and not set.
The punctuation after a note's mark or a citation is set before it,
as Chicago has it, and
.I refer
moves it again as its style needs.
A key that is a heading's, table's or figure's label,
.BR [@sec:method] ,
is a cross-reference to it
.RB ( "\e*[ref sec:method]" );
.B [](#label)
is too.
.B $...$
is eqn's mathematics, in eqn's language, not TeX's
.RB ( "$x sup 2$" ).
.B `...`{=troff}
is troff as written.
Two spaces or a backslash at a line's end break it.
Entities
.RB ( &amp; ,
.BR &mdash; ,
.BR &#8212; )
are their characters; a backslash before a mark is the mark.
.SS Typography
.B --
is an en dash,
.B ---
an em dash,
.B ...
an ellipsis.
A straight double quote is the first quotation mark and a straight
single quote, where it is not an apostrophe, the second (a quotation
within a quotation):
.B gb
sets them as British, ‘ ’ and “ ”,
.B us
as American, “ ” and ‘ ’, and
.B none
leaves them straight.
The style is
.BR -q 's,
or the front matter's
.BR quotes: ,
or its
.B lang:
.RB ( en-US
and
.B en-CA
American, any other English British), or that of the curly marks the
text already has; failing all of these, British, and said.
Curly marks are left as they are written.
An apostrophe before a word
.RB ( "'tis" )
is taken for a quotation mark: write it
.B ’
or
.BR \e' .
.PP
.B -k
prints the front matter's value for
.I key
and nothing else:
.B "-k macros"
the class as it is resolved,
.B "-k bibliography"
and
.BR "-k citestyle" ,
for
.IR book (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
book proposal.md
book -f -p works.bib thesis.md
md2troff -m article -q us paper.md >paper.ms
md2troff paper.md | book2tex -m article -o paper.tex
.EE
.PP
A paper's head:
.EX
---
title: Setting a Paragraph Whole
author:
  - name: A. Typesetter
    affiliation: InferNode Project
lang: en-GB
macros: article
bibliography: works.bib
---
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/md2troff.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR book (1),
.IR refer (1),
.IR troff (6)
.SH BUGS
TeX's mathematics is not translated into eqn's.
A citation's prefix, definition lists and HTML are not set.
An apostrophe before a word is taken for a quotation mark.
